ShapeShifter 3.20 beta 2 - a Macintosh II emulator for the Amiga

ShapeShifter runs the Macintosh system (System 7 to Mac OS 8.1) and its
programs on an Amiga with a 68020 or better, next to your Amiga programs.

THIS IS A BETA. It has run on few Amigas so far (see "Tested" below).
Keep copies of Mac disks you care about, and read the part on ReserveLow
before you let it into your Startup-Sequence.

To install, double-click Install_ShapeShifter. It copies the program, the
manual and the language files into a drawer of your choice. Run it again
to update: settings, ROM and Mac disks are kept.

You also need, and ShapeShifter does not contain:
 - a Macintosh ROM file (512 KB or 1 MB) read from a Mac you own
 - a Macintosh system to install, for example from a system CD

At its first start ShapeShifter offers to set itself up. The manual is
ShapeShifter_E.guide (English) and ShapeShifter.guide (German). In the
English one, "Quick start" takes you from this archive to the Mac desktop,
"Troubleshooting" helps when it does not start, and "Settings at a glance"
lists every setting with its default; the "Defaults" button in the
settings window chooses settings that fit your Amiga. The German manual
has the same chapters ("Schnellstart", "Fehlersuche", "Einstellungen im
Ueberblick").

The low memory (ReserveLow)
---------------------------
ShapeShifter needs the lowest memory of the Amiga free from boot on.
ReserveLow does that: run it once after the Amiga is switched on (it
restarts the Amiga), or let the installer put "C:ReserveLow QUIET" at the
top of your Startup-Sequence. The installer suggests "No" for now.

ReserveLow is new. If your Amiga does not start with it: hold the LEFT
MOUSE BUTTON down while the Amiga starts or resets. ReserveLow then does
nothing, the Amiga starts as usual, and you can take the line out of
S:Startup-Sequence (the file as it was is
S:Startup-Sequence.before-ShapeShifter). Switching the Amiga off also
removes ReserveLow from memory. Other software uses the same button as
its "not this time" key (the PrismRTG graphics driver, for one), so a
start with the left button held is a safe start with all of it off.

PrepareEmul, the tool of ShapeShifter 3.11, is not in this archive any
more. ReserveLow cannot do its work on an Amiga whose only fast memory is
on Zorro cards (it says so and changes nothing): use PrepareEmul from the
3.11 archive there. The manual has the details under "Reserving the low
memory".

The Mac disk tools (drawer MacDiskTools, optional)
--------------------------------------------------
MacBrowse copies files between the Amiga and a Mac disk image (.hfv and
others); MacMount with L:MacHFS-Handler shows an image as an Amiga
volume. They work on the image file while ShapeShifter is NOT running.
See MacDiskTools/MacBrowse.readme. They are new as well: mount read-only
(MacMount HFV0: image RO) or work on a copy until you trust them.

Tested
------
 - Amiga 1200, 68030 + 68882, Kickstart 3.2.3, AGA: Mac OS 8.0 and 8.1,
   sound through the Amiga's own audio (heard), a Mac disk on a SCSI
   drive, the installer, ReserveLow
 - Amiga 4000, 68060, Kickstart 3.2.3, graphics card and AGA: Mac OS 8.0
   and 8.1, TCP/IP through a SANA-II driver, sound through AHI (recorded
   to a file), ReserveLow
 - The same Amiga 4000 with Kickstart 3.1, AGA: Mac OS 8.1
 - Amiga 2000, 68030 accelerator (no FPU), Kickstart 3.2.3, ECS and a
   Picasso II+ card: System 7.5 in 2, 4 and 16 colours on the ECS
   screen, System 7.5 and Mac OS 8.1 in 256 and thousands of colours
   on the card, sound, TCP/IP (DHCP) through a SANA-II driver shared
   with the Amiga's own stack, the installer, ReserveLow, the Mac
   disk tools
 - WinUAE: A1200 68030 with Kickstart 3.1 and 3.2.3, A4000 68060;
   System 7.5, Mac OS 8.0 and 8.1; the installer on Workbench 3.1 and 3.2

Known problems
--------------
Not tested, so expect surprises and please report them:
 - 68020 and 68040 processors, OCS screens, the DraCo.
 - Long sessions (many hours).
 - CD music on real hardware.
 - AGA screens whose width is not a multiple of 64 (800x600, for one)
   together with "MMU refresh" or with the Mac switching colour depth.
   Without those two they work.
 - "Format..." for device disks above 2 GB, and Disk First Aid on a disk
   that ShapeShifter formatted.
 - The left mouse button of ReserveLow with a real button: Amiga 4000
   only.
 - A cold start of ReserveLow under Kickstart 3.1 on real hardware.

Seen:
 - A Mac disk image on a Fast File System partition of a slow drive
   makes the Mac start extremely slowly. ShapeShifter measures this and
   warns before the Mac starts. Put the image on a PFS3 or SFS
   partition, or use a device disk.
 - A settings file from 3.11 may name a screen mode that no longer
   exists: ShapeShifter says so and opens the settings. Click "Defaults"
   or choose a screen mode on the Graphics tab, and save.
 - Each SCSI ID that is switched on but has no drive adds a few seconds
   of grey screen before the Mac starts (3.11 took minutes). Switch
   unused IDs off on the SCSI tab.
 - The extras of the 3.11 archive (PrepareEmul, SaveROM, KickShifter,
   Mac-Handler, the external video drivers) are not in this archive;
   those of 3.11 still work.

To remove ShapeShifter, delete its drawer, take the ReserveLow line out
of S:Startup-Sequence and delete C:ReserveLow, C:MacMount and
L:MacHFS-Handler.

